Subject: Add the `virt` profile: the Comet image for QEMU's arm64 virt machine

The Comet image (Mecha kernel, Mechanix session and apps) built for QEMU's
generic `virt` machine instead of the i.MX8MP board:

- mkosi.profiles/virt.conf; the Mecha kernel and Comet package files now match
  `comet` or `virt` (triggering `|` conditions).
- mkosi.extra.virt: simulated hardware (comet-simd: gpio-sim header, vcan can0,
  mock UPower/power-profiles over D-Bus) driven from the host over virtio-serial,
  and app-only mode (comet-app.service).
- mkosi.postinst.chroot: virt session fix-ups (software EGL opt-ins, Virtual-1
  connector, gpio group).
- mechanix-session: app-only branch, inert unless /run/mechanix-app exists.

Upstream: mecha-org/mecha-make, against pre-release b226b42.

